#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Control the Samsung QN55QN700B (Tizen) TV from this workstation.

The TV is the DeskMeet1 8K monitor (192.168.1.250). This drives it without the
physical remote through the interfaces Tizen exposes on the LAN:

  REST        http://TV:8001/api/v2/        device info, application launch
  WebSocket   wss://TV:8002/api/v2/channels/samsung.remote.control
                                             remote keys, apps, browser, text
  UPnP DMR    http://TV:9197/dmr             RenderingControl volume get/set
  Wake-on-LAN UDP/9 magic packet             power on from standby

Usage: curiosity-tv [--host IP] [--mac MAC] [--timeout S] [--json] COMMAND ...
       status | on | off | pair | key KEY... | input hdmi1..4|source
       volume up|down|mute [N] | volume get | volume set N
       channel up|down|N | home | back | apps | launch APP | browse URL
       text STRING | cursor move DX DY | cursor click|rightclick

`status` needs no token. Everything over the WebSocket needs the pairing token,
looked up in this order and never printed or put on a command line:
  1. $CURIOSITY_TV_TOKEN
  2. $XDG_STATE_HOME/curiosity-tv/token (0600; default ~/.local/state)
  3. Azure Key Vault (through `az`; the value is then cached as in 2). The
     vault and secret names come from $CURIOSITY_TV_KEY_VAULT and
     $CURIOSITY_TV_KEY_VAULT_SECRET (default secret deskmeet-samsung-tv-ws-token)
     or from /etc/curiosity/samsung-tv.env, which the role renders.
If the TV issues a new token on connect it is written to the cache only (0600)
and a notice asks you to sync it to Key Vault.

Every network operation (REST, UPnP, WebSocket connect/send/receive/close)
runs under a hard wall-clock deadline (--timeout, default 10 s), so no
subcommand can hang; websocket-client answers TV pings inside recv(), which
would otherwise defeat a per-socket timeout. `apps` waits --wait seconds
(default 8) for ed.installedApp.get, which 2020+ firmware often ignores, then
probes the known app ids over REST.

Exit status: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error, 3 not authorised/no token,
4 timed out.
Managed by the curiosity workstation role.
"""
